From 3e00c8a4f73a08abe159d8a9a476a0c32dc951cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Santos <lsantos7654@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 7 May 2026 21:58:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 19/21] File-write hook + hivemind memory-compaction auto-spawn
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a scoped post-write hook to the plugin API and uses it from the
new hivemind-memory plugin to auto-spawn the
`hivemind-memory-daemon` system_templated agent when an agent's
`short_memory.md` crosses the configured byte threshold.

Engine-side: `onFileWrite` plugin hook
--------------------------------------

Plugins declare path patterns at registration time and receive only
matching writes. Non-memory writes never enter the plugin runtime —
the dispatch short-circuits when the registry is empty.

  packages/plugin/src/index.ts:
    Hooks.onFileWrite?: { patterns: string[]; handler(input) }

  packages/opencode/src/plugin/index.ts:
    Plugin.notifyFileWrite(input) walks loaded hooks, matches patterns
    via Bun.Glob, dispatches handlers. Errors logged + swallowed so a
    misbehaving plugin can't break the originating tool call.

  packages/opencode/src/tool/{write,edit}.ts:
    After a successful write, call Plugin.notifyFileWrite with the
    absolute path, sessionID, post-write byte count, and tool name.

Engine-side: hivemind-memory plugin
-----------------------------------

  packages/opencode/src/plugin/hivemind-memory.ts:
    Registers onFileWrite for **/hivemind/memory/**/short_memory.md.
    On match: read threshold from hivemind.json (cached, mtime-
    invalidated, default 8192 bytes); single typed lookup of writer
    session for parent_id; recursion guard via writer.agent ===
    "hivemind-memory-daemon"; spawn daemon as depth-1 child of main
    via client.session.create with structured metadata.

Tests
-----

  test/plugin/file-write-hook.test.ts (5):
    pattern match dispatches; non-match skips; zero-plugin no-op;
    handler errors don't propagate; Edit fires the same hook.

  test/plugin/hivemind-memory.test.ts (3):
    sub-threshold doesn't spawn; over-threshold spawns daemon as
    sibling-of-writer (child of main) with structured metadata
    populated; non-memory paths ignored.

Spawn properties
----------------

  - Depth-1 invariant preserved: daemon.parent_id == writer.parent_id
    (or writer.id if writer IS main), no chain walking.
  - Visible in main's subagents pill (TUI footer auto-refetches on
    session.created/deleted events).
  - Killable: cascades with main via existing patch 0010 mechanism.
  - One-shot: daemon completes one compaction pass and exits; no loop,
    no scheduler, no external dependency.
  - Recursion guard: when the daemon writes back to short_memory.md
    during compaction, hook fires again and skips (writer is daemon).
